                    <div class="mb-10 rounded-[15px] bg-[#EFF6FF] p-5 md:p-8" data-anim="">
                        <h2 class="mb-4 font-fraunces text-[26px] font-normal leading-[1.17] tracking-[-0.01em] text-[#0A0A09] md:text-[32px]">
                            Key takeaways</h2>
                        <div class="blog-takeaways text-[17px] leading-[1.4] text-[#0A0A09] md:text-[18px]">
                            <ul><li><p>Remove contaminated clothing immediately and flush with water for 15-20 minutes minimum</p></li><li><p>Never neutralize acid burns with alkali or vice versa - this creates dangerous heat reactions</p></li><li><p>Chemical burns continue damaging tissue after initial contact, making speed crucial</p></li><li><p>Seek immediate medical attention for burns larger than 3 inches or involving eyes/airways</p></li></ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                

                

                


                <div id="blog-article" class="blog-article">
                    
                        
                            
    
    <p>Chemical burns are medical emergencies that demand immediate, specific treatment to prevent permanent tissue damage and life-threatening complications. Unlike thermal burns that cause instant damage, chemical burns continue destroying healthy tissue until the caustic substance is completely removed from the skin. Whether from workplace accidents or household incidents, knowing proper first aid for chemical burns can mean the difference between minor injury and permanent scarring. If you experience a chemical burn, Doctronic's 24/7 AI consultations can provide immediate guidance on when to seek emergency care and proper aftercare&nbsp;steps.</p>


                        
                    
                        
                            


